  "content": {
    "title": "Amy Madigan Walks the Oscars Red Carpet With Husband Ed Harris—40 Years After Their First Attendance",
    "text": "\"Hearst Magazines and Yahoo may earn commission or revenue on some items through these links.\"Get ready, Weapons fans—Amy Madigan has officially arrived to the 2026 Academy Awards.Tonight, the Chicago-born star arrived to the ceremony in yet another statement-making look, which was courtesy of Dior. It was a suit, but not just your typical suit—this one featured a striking blazer completely covered in black-and-gold feather paillettes, creating a dappled effect.Amy Madigan at the 98th Academy Awards.Frazer Harrison - Getty ImagesThe impressionist coat was paired with stark-black slacks and pointy pumps to match, allowing the statement piece to really shine. However, for another fiery touch, the actor wore a pair of round glasses with bright-orange lenses.Madigan wears a striking look courtesy of Dior.Frazer Harrison - Getty ImagesIt seems fitting that Madigan chose such a showstopping ensemble, given that she’s making history at the 98th Oscars.With her nod for Best Actress in a Supporting Role, thanks to her performance as Gladys in Weapons, Madigan became the female actor with the largest gap between nominations. The last time she was nominated was in the same category, 40 years back, at the 1986 Academy Awards. She received the nod for her performance as Sunny Mackenzie-Sobel in Twice in a Lifetime.Amy Madigan at the 1986 Oscars with her husband, Ed Harris.Ron Galella, Ltd. - Getty ImagesIn an interview with People, Madigan commented on the achievement, saying: “I’m just kind of stunned by the whole journey that I've been on. This is just... another piece of it that I was not expecting, but I’m just very happy and gratified and it’s just a reflection on the film Weapons and how people are responding to it. So that—nothing is a better feeling than that.”She later added: “People always say, ‘If you have a dream, follow it,’ et cetera. But those are true things when actors and writers and directors get up there and say that because it’s a long, arduous trip, it takes a lot of work. Don’t be deterred. And it’s really true. When a good piece of material comes by, the actors, they want to grab it by the throat. It’s exciting. That’s why we do what we do. So it’s all been kind of a whirlwind, but very exciting.”Madigan walked the red carpet with her husband, Ed Harris.Arturo Holmes - Getty ImagesThis evening, Madigan returns to the ceremony with her husband of 42 years, Ed Harris, who accompanied her when she received her first nomination back in ’86. Talk about a full circle moment.You Might Also Like",
